website footer; the Stable Audio Open model is published by stabilityai.","Access type","pipeline source","access","section",[75],{"_58":76,"_25":77,"_78":79},"Audio tools source","https://github.com/Stability-AI/stable-audio-tools","note","MIT-licensed training and inference code; Stable Audio Open 1.0 weights are separately gated and governed by the model's Community License. No complete game project.","local tool","demo",[83],{"_58":84,"_25":85,"_78":86},"Local audio demo setup","https://github.com/Stability-AI/stable-audio-tools#interface","Download and run the official Gradio audio interface locally; this link is setup guidance, not a hosted playable game.","tutorial",[89],{"_58":90,"_25":91,"_78":92},"Local inference and WAV export","https://huggingface.co/stabilityai/stable-audio-open-1.0#usage","Official model usage examples for stable-audio-tools and Diffusers.","Source reviewed","2026-10-19","verified","metadata","Year","2024","year","list","Tracks","ordered",false,[106,107],"dimensions","2D","3D","Development stages",[111],"stages","Assets & animation","Topics",[115,116,117,118,119],"tags","Text-to-audio","Sound effects","Field recordings","Model weights","Local inference","Further reading",[122,123,124],{"_58":129,"_25":85},{"_58":127,"_25":128},{"_58":125,"_25":126},"Stable Audio Open model license","https://huggingface.co/stabilityai/stable-audio-open-1.0/blob/main/LICENSE.md","Research paper","https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.14358","Local demo setup","Project source",[132],{"_58":130,"_25":133},"https://huggingface.co/stabilityai/stable-audio-open-1.0","Why it belongs here","Generates up to 47 seconds of stereo audio at 44.1 kHz, with examples for local inference and WAV export. The official audio-tools repository includes a local Gradio interface. The model works best with English descriptions, is stronger at sound effects and field recordings than music, and cannot produce realistic vocals. Model access requires accepting its terms and sharing contact in